  "limits": [
    "Actual web imports a saved file as a new budget; native restores its own portable backup in place. Equivalent1104 financial rows, different archive bytes and identity semantics.",
    "Reuses the restarted opening containers and their other fixture budgets. Fresh browser profile per sample; source adds20 files, native restores one cloned target20 times. No isolated-host or equal-server-memory-state claim.",
    "Initial baseline pilot waited for a file chooser before pressing Select file. Second pilot completed UI recovery but native financial checker requested2000 rows despite the1000-row public page cap. Both excluded; final checker uses snapshot-bound paging. No product correction.",
    "Same native backup is staged repeatedly; one retained stage ID is reused. First review868ms/activation1945ms; repeated-review median99ms. These are repeat-snapshot distributions, not20 independent cold validation runs."
  ],
